{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3a33af34e4d8a7902accddd8202823e2b0ce620ff5465512410b87271857e67b","digest":{"component_or_area":"mapping seam documentation and portability","key_entities":["[tool.rebar.mapping]","docs/config.md","docs/mapping-seam.md","docs/README.md","CHANGELOG","status axis","type axis","link axis","priority axis","create_defaults axis",".bridge_state/projects.json","probe command"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","portability","mapping seam","provider-neutral","migration safety","reuse","configuration"],"propositions":["The mapping seam config surface and behaviors (breadcrumb, replay, probe) lack authoritative end-to-end documentation for operators and future integrators.","The plan-review portability criterion requires that no capability's sole trigger is a specific CI provider; the mapping seam must function in diverse or provider-absent environments.","Future integrations (Linear, GitLab, GitHub-Issues) need a documented provider-neutral reuse contract to build against the mapping seam core.","The feature is additive and backward-compatible; an absent [tool.rebar.mapping] section must reproduce current hardcoded behavior and rollback requires only section deletion.","All mapping behavior is covered by injected-transport unit tests requiring no live Jira or specific CI provider, substantiating the portability claim."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787759992079330001,"uuid":"fd3ea8a4-3796-4300-ae00-2f87ccd1226f"}